{"causes": ["The decline of the Pagan Kingdom created a power vacuum in Lower Burma, allowing regional Mon states like Martaban to emerge.", "The rising expansionist ambitions of the Sukhothai Kingdom threatened Martaban's autonomy, necessitating a strong leader.", "Queen Sanda Min Hla's political influence and strategic maneuvering placed Binnya E Law on the throne to secure Mon interests."], "effects": ["Binnya E Law's victory in 1331 permanently ended Martaban's tributary status to the Sukhothai Kingdom.", "His reign fostered a period of political independence and relative stability for the Mon kingdom of Martaban.", "The successful defense against Sukhothai solidified Martaban's position as a regional power in mainland Southeast Asia for several decades."], "relationships": [{"sourceSlug": "sanda-min-hla", "sourceName": "Queen Sanda Min Hla", "verb": "CAUSES", "targetSlug": "binnya-e-law", "targetName": "Binnya E Law", "context": "Queen Sanda Min Hla orchestrated Binnya E Law's ascension to the throne of Martaban in 1330."}, {"sourceSlug": "binnya-e-law", "sourceName": "Binnya E Law", "verb": "PARTICIPATES_IN", "targetSlug": "sukhothai-martaban-war-1330-1331", "targetName": "Sukhothai-Martaban War (1330-1331)", "context": "Binnya E Law led Martaban's forces to repel the Sukhothai invasion between 1330 and 1331."}, {"sourceSlug": "binnya-e-law", "sourceName": "Binnya E Law", "verb": "OCCURS_IN", "targetSlug": "martaban-kingdom", "targetName": "Martaban Kingdom", "context": "Binnya E Law ruled as king of the Martaban Kingdom from 1330 until 1348."}, {"sourceSlug": "binnya-e-law", "sourceName": "Binnya E Law", "verb": "TRANSFORMS", "targetSlug": "martaban-sukhothai-relations", "targetName": "Martaban-Sukhothai Relations", "context": "Binnya E Law's decisive victory in 1331 transformed Martaban's status from a Sukhothai tributary to an independent entity."}, {"sourceSlug": "binnya-e-law", "sourceName": "Binnya E Law", "verb": "SUCCEEDS", "targetSlug": "khun-law-martaban", "targetName": "King Hkun Law of Martaban", "context": "Binnya E Law, son of King Hkun Law, succeeded him on the throne of Martaban in 1330."}], "places": [{"name": "Martaban, Burma", "role": "Capital City, Seat of Power"}, {"name": "Lower Burma, Burma", "role": "Region of Rule"}, {"name": "Sukhothai, Siam", "role": "Invading Kingdom's Capital"}], "texts": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Binnya E Law", "type": "Reference article", "slug": "binnya-e-law"}], "externalLinks": ["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q2903962", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Binnya_E_Law"], "tags": ["Monarchs & Rulers", "political-systems", "empire-and-colonialism", "geopolitical-linkage"], "thumbnailUrl": "", "quote": "", "legacySummary": "", "historicalSignificance": {"significanceScore": 7, "significanceNarrative": "Binnya E Law's successful defense against the Sukhothai invasion in 1330-1331 definitively ended Martaban's tributary status and secured its independence for decades, reshaping the regional balance of power in mainland Southeast Asia. His reign allowed the Mon people to maintain distinct political and cultural autonomy amidst larger empires.", "significanceCategory": "regional"}, "_editLog": [{"timestamp": "2026-11-14T08:15:55Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#43574567599", "field": "summary", "oldValue": "Binnya E Law was king of Martaban from 1330 to 1348. Placed on the throne by his half-sister Queen Sanda Min Hla, this son of King Hkun Law defeated Sukhothai's invasion in 1330–1331, ending Martaban's tributary status to the Siamese kingdom.", "newValue": "Binnya E Law reigned as king of Martaban (Lower Burma) from 1330 until his death in 1348, a pivotal period that saw the reassertion of Mon sovereignty against encroaching Siamese power. His ascension, orchestrated by his influential half-sister Queen Sanda Min Hla, marked a crucial turn in the political landscape of the Mon-speaking regions, solidifying Martaban's independence from the rising influence of the Sukhothai Kingdom. His reign laid the groundwork for a more stable and autonomous Mon state, distinct from both Siamese and Burman ambitions, contributing significantly to the regional balance of power during the 14th century.

Upon assuming the throne, Binnya E Law immediately faced a formidable challenge: a large-scale invasion from the Sukhothai Kingdom in 1330–1331, aimed at re-establishing its suzerainty over Martaban. Demonstrating military acumen and strategic resolve, Binnya E Law successfully repelled these Siamese forces, a decisive victory that permanently severed Martaban's long-standing tributary obligations to Sukhothai. This military triumph was not merely defensive; it affirmed Martaban's status as an independent regional power, allowing the kingdom to pursue its own diplomatic and economic interests free from external domination.

Binnya E Law's reign ensured that Martaban would continue to be a significant player in mainland Southeast Asia for decades, postponing its eventual absorption into larger regional empires. His successful defense against Sukhothai created a precedent for Mon resistance and contributed to a distinct cultural and political identity that persisted through subsequent centuries. The stability achieved under his rule allowed for continued prosperity in the key port city of Martaban, a vital hub for maritime trade between India, China, and the Malay Archipelago."}, {"timestamp": "2026-11-14T08:15:55Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#43574567599", "field": "detailsJson.causes", "oldValue": [{"title": "Medieval era: interplay of religious authority, feudal governance, and trade network expansion", "type": "EventWindow", "year": "1308-03-21, Mottama"}, {"title": "Dynastic succession and sovereign authority traditions", "type": "Idea", "year": "1308-03-21, Mottama"}], "newValue": ["The decline of the Pagan Kingdom created a power vacuum in Lower Burma, allowing regional Mon states like Martaban to emerge.", "The rising expansionist ambitions of the Sukhothai Kingdom threatened Martaban's autonomy, necessitating a strong leader.", "Queen Sanda Min Hla's political influence and strategic maneuvering placed Binnya E Law on the throne to secure Mon interests."]}, {"timestamp": "2026-11-14T08:15:55Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#43574567599", "field": "detailsJson.effects", "oldValue": [{"title": "Established dynastic legacies and territorial boundaries", "type": "Idea", "year": "1348"}, {"title": "Contributed to synthesis of classical and religious thought informing Renaissance and Reformati", "type": "Movement", "year": "1348"}], "newValue": ["Binnya E Law's victory in 1331 permanently ended Martaban's tributary status to the Sukhothai Kingdom.", "His reign fostered a period of political independence and relative stability for the Mon kingdom of Martaban.", "Th